# Test: every locally registered data command reaches the pipe layer
# QUESTION: Does the shipped ze CLI deliver every registered local-data answer
# through a real output pipe, including caller-held standalone inputs?
# A unit test cannot prove binary composition, process stdio delivery or the
# ze cli -c entry point. The AST registry test separately proves population.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-10 and AC-45 S5 -- actual local entry-to-pipe semantics.
# PREVENTS: a registered owner remaining unreachable, empty fabricated answers,
# ignored caller bytes, and a new registration without executable evidence.

option=timeout:value=45s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test local-data-coverage
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=COVERED: clear debug [done]
expect=stdout:contains=COVERED: delete debug module [done]
expect=stdout:contains=COVERED: delete debug profile name [done]
expect=stdout:contains=COVERED: doctor [done]
expect=stdout:contains=COVERED: help ai [done]
expect=stdout:contains=COVERED: help command [done]
expect=stdout:contains=COVERED: request support archive [done]
expect=stdout:contains=COVERED: request wireguard keypair [done]
expect=stdout:contains=COVERED: set debug active name [done]
expect=stdout:contains=COVERED: set debug module [done]
expect=stdout:contains=COVERED: set debug profile name [done]
expect=stdout:contains=COVERED: set debug timeout [done]
